\n[Navbar](/vibe-hub/navbar?lang=en)[Sticky](/vibe-hub/sticky?lang=en)\n\n## You can say this to an AI Agent\n\n> “\n> Use a top-navigation layout for the content site: put brand, five primary destinations, and search in the top bar, constrain article width, and collect secondary entries on mobile. Verify current-page state, long titles, and sticky offset.\n\n### When to use it\n\n- Marketing site\n\n◆ logoProduct · Docs · PricingFree trial\n- Product with a few main sections\n\nmax-width: 1120px · margin: 0 auto\n- Content that needs full page width\n\nTop bar · position: sticky\n- Simple cross-page navigation\n\nCreate project\n\n### When NOT to use it\n\n- Squeeze many deep sections into one row\n\nHomeProductApproachDocsBlogPricingAboutCareersEvents\n- Hide the active destination\n- Let navigation wrap into an accidental second line\n\nDashboardProjectsTasksFilesMembersCalendarReportsMessagesSettingsTrash\n- Copy the desktop row unchanged onto a phone\n\nTop bar and body share the same background colorLacks visual layering\n\nAnatomy\n\n****Content areaFooter · Copyright and secondary links\n\n1HeaderHolds the brand, navigation, and primary actions; make it sticky when needed\n\n2MainThe page’s main content, centered with a maximum width and side whitespace\n\n3FooterHolds copyright, regulatory information, and secondary links\n\nVariants\n\nStatic\n\nFor a short page that does not need persistent navigation\n\nSticky\n\nWhen navigation should remain available while users scroll through a long page\n\nStacked\n\nWhen the navigation has too many items for a single row\n\nTypical use cases\n\nCompany site\n\n**◆ Late-Night Frontend**\n        HomepageColumnWeeklyAbout\n        Subscribe\n\n      \nHow I used AI to build a website in one week\n\n          \nFrontend notes · Yesterday · 8 minutes to read\n\n        \nFive CSS Grid layouts you’ll use again and again\n\n          \nTutorial · 3 days ago · Read in 12 minutes\n\nSaaS product\n\n**▲ Yunxie Flow**\n        ProductsSolutionsPricingDocuments\n        Log in\n        Free trial\n\n      \nMake team collaboration as easy as chat\n\n        \nTasks, documents, and schedules in one place, get started in 5 minutes\n\n        Get started for free\n        Watch demo →\n\nPortfolio\n\n**▮ DevDocs**\n        GuidelinesAPIExamplesCommunity\n        \n        GitHub\n\n      \nQuick start\n\n        \n        \n        \nnpm install vibekit\n\nSimple dashboard\n\n**● Innovation Conference**\n        AgendaGuestsPrevious ReviewFAQ\n        Register now\n\n      \n2026 Summer Session · August 15 · Shanghai\n        \nDesigner’s AI Workflow Conference\n\n        \n12 practical sharing sessions a day, early bird tickets are limited to 500\n\n        \nGet early bird tickets\n\nRecommended tool\n[Web fine-tuning tool · Selector Pro\n\n## Select page elements for precise AI edits\n\nClick a button, text, or card, note the change, then copy its exact location to AI.\nOpen Selector Pro website↗\n\nyour-site.com\n\n**Button · Get started**Use a smaller radius\n\nButton · Get started**Copied for AI**](https://selector-pro.org/)\n\nFurther reading\n\n[Menu-Design Checklist: 17 UX GuidelinesNN/g ↗](https://www.nngroup.com/articles/menu-design/)"}